<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy · Donna Moneypenny" %>

<main class="legal">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: October 11, 2026</p>

  <p>
    Donna Moneypenny is a private, non-commercial personal finance tool. It is used by its
    owner only, to keep track of their own income and expenses. It is not offered to the public,
    and no one else can sign up for it.
  </p>

  <h2>What data is processed</h2>
  <p>
    With the owner's explicit consent, given at their bank, the app reads account information
    from the owner's own bank accounts through Enable Banking Oy, a licensed account information
    service provider. This can include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>account details such as account name, number (IBAN) and currency</li>
    <li>balances</li>
    <li>transactions, including dates, amounts, counterparties and payment messages</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why it is processed</h2>
  <p>
    Only to show the owner an overview of their own finances: categorising spending, tracking
    income and producing personal summaries. The data is not used for any other purpose. It is
    never sold or shared with third parties, and it is not used for advertising or profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Data is stored in a database on a server operated for the owner by Hetzner Online GmbH in
    Helsinki, Finland (EU). Connections to the app are encrypted with HTTPS.
  </p>

  <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Data is kept for as long as the owner uses the app. Access to the bank expires automatically
    when the consent given at the bank ends, and the owner can revoke it at any time through
    their bank or Enable Banking. Stored data is deleted when the owner deletes it or stops
    using the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    The only person whose data is processed is the owner, who has full control over it and can
    view, export or delete it at any time.
  </p>

  <p class="legal-footer"><%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path %></p>
</main>
